  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (avgpool, concat) achieved 0.512 acc at 4.33 GPU hrs, clearly outperforming config_010 (transformer, concat) at 0.471 acc and 9.06 GPU hrs. This establishes avgpool aggregation as the superior choice and concat fusion as a strong baseline. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining scgpt RNA and resnet50 image features with avgpool aggregation? This directly tests the fusion mechanism, an important design axis not yet explored. Rationale: config_011 is the most natural and cheap extension of our current best (same architecture, only fusion changes from concat→weighted), expected cost ~4.3 GPU hrs (similar to config_005). With 7 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out weighted fusion early lets us lock in the best fusion strategy before exploring larger changes (e.g., imagenet_vit_l, different RNA encoders) in later, more expensive experiments. This balances exploitation of the promising avgpool+scgpt+resnet50 direction with targeted uncertainty reduction on a key design choice."
